{
  "info": {
    "name": "P2 – Content Decision Ledger",
    "description": "Drives the four input topics through the existing services and queries the ledger.\n\nIMPORTANT — contentId convention enforced by the `verification-activity-monitor` branch:\n• verification-service:  contentId = 'content-<sha256(contentUrl)[:16]>'\n• reporting-service:     contentId = postId\n\nTo make verification + reporting events correlate on the SAME ledger key, the flow below first reads the derived contentId from the verification record, then uses it as the postId when filing the report.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "content_ledger",       "value": "http://localhost:8085" },
    { "key": "verification_service", "value": "http://localhost:8002" },
    { "key": "reporting_service",    "value": "http://localhost:8003" },
    { "key": "user_service",         "value": "http://localhost:8001" },
    { "key": "user_id",        "value": "" },
    { "key": "verification_id","value": "" },
    { "key": "content_id",     "value": "" },
    { "key": "content_url",    "value": "https://example.com/post-demo-1" },
    { "key": "report_id",      "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Ledger – Health & Stream State",
      "item": [
        { "name": "Actuator health",
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{content_ledger}}/actuator/health" } },
        { "name": "Streams runtime state",
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{content_ledger}}/api/health/stream" } }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Ledger – Interactive Queries",
      "item": [
        { "name": "List all tracked content",
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{content_ledger}}/api/content?limit=100&withState=true" } },
        { "name": "Get state by contentId",
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{content_ledger}}/api/content/{{content_id}}/state" } },
        { "name": "Get full decision trace",
          "request": { "method": "GET", "url": "{{content_ledger}}/api/content/{{content_id}}/decision-trace" } }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "End-to-End Flow – run in order",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Register a user",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "exec": [
            "var j = pm.response.json();",
            "if (j.processInstanceKey) pm.collectionVariables.set('user_id', j.processInstanceKey);"
          ]}}],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{user_service}}/users",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"alice\",\n  \"password\": \"secret\"\n}" }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Submit verification (verification-service derives contentId from contentUrl)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "exec": [
            "var j = pm.response.json();",
            "if (j.verificationId) pm.collectionVariables.set('verification_id', j.verificationId);"
          ]}}],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{verification_service}}/verifications",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"userId\": \"{{user_id}}\",\n  \"contentUrl\": \"{{content_url}}\",\n  \"contentTitle\": \"Demo article\",\n  \"peerMode\": \"auto-approve\"\n}" }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Read back the derived contentId (sha256-hashed)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "exec": [
            "var j = pm.response.json();",
            "if (j.contentId) pm.collectionVariables.set('content_id', j.contentId);",
            "console.log('content_id =', j.contentId);"
          ]}}],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{verification_service}}/verifications/{{verification_id}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4. File a report using postId == contentId (so it correlates in the ledger)",
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "exec": [
            "var j = pm.response.json();",
            "if (j.reportId) pm.collectionVariables.set('report_id', j.reportId);"
          ]}}],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{reporting_service}}/reports",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"reporterId\": \"{{user_id}}\",\n  \"postId\": \"{{content_id}}\",\n  \"postOwnerId\": \"{{user_id}}\",\n  \"reason\": \"spam\",\n  \"objectionMode\": \"manual\"\n}" }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Optional – submit an objection (triggers objection-approved if approved)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{reporting_service}}/reports/{{report_id}}/objection",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"explanation\": \"Content is factually correct.\"\n}" }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Query the ledger – decision trace for {{content_id}}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{content_ledger}}/api/content/{{content_id}}/decision-trace"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
